invariant: INV-17
file: src/aead_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh aead-avx2
reason: aead_avx2_open returns without VZEROALL. Its last step is the
  keystream of the rest of the message, so ymm0 to ymm15 hold keystream and
  state words, which give the key. Every tag and byte is still right.
  bin/aead_avx2_equiv_test sets every bit of the sixteen registers, calls
  the entry and requires every stored word zero. The file has a body on
  x86-64 alone, so the script builds the binary for x86-64 and runs it
  under qemu-x86_64.

--- old
    xor_message(input, pass_counter(passes - 1), ct + hashed, pt + hashed, n - hashed);
    ct_wipe(input, sizeof input);
    _mm256_zeroall();
--- new
    xor_message(input, pass_counter(passes - 1), ct + hashed, pt + hashed, n - hashed);
    ct_wipe(input, sizeof input);
